# ThreadSanitizer suppressions of the tsan presets (TSAN_OPTIONS in CMakePresets.json). Only code
# that is not the project's belongs here, each entry with why: our own code is never suppressed.

# Mesa's lavapipe, the software Vulkan of the CI: its rasterizer threads (llvmpipe) are not
# instrumented, and ThreadSanitizer, which sees their pthread calls only, reports races on Mesa's
# own mutexes (a mutex destroyed by one of its threads while another one leaves it).
race:libvulkan_lvp.so
# Its rasterizer threads compile shaders through Mesa's LLVM (llvmpipe's JIT), as uninstrumented: a race
# reported in LLVM's own string maps, between an llvmpipe thread and a Vulkan call of the main thread
# (vkCreateImage), shows lavapipe's frames in neither stack, inlined away.
race:libLLVM.so
